--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Why this project is GPL
    chessops (GPL-3.0-or-later) — https://github.com/niklasf/chessops
    implements the rules VelaChess is built on: legality and move
    generation, SAN and UCI, FEN and EPD, and the PGN tree with variations
    that the repertoire model depends on. libs/chess is a façade over it
    and nothing else in the workspace imports it directly. It is linked
    into this program, and so this program carries the same licence.

Stockfish — GPL-3.0-or-later
    https://stockfishchess.org/
    https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish

    Used for position analysis, and NOT linked into this program: the
    engine runs as a separate process, communicated with over the UCI
    protocol on stdin/stdout. apps/worker spawns whatever the ENGINE_CMD
    environment variable names; the published Docker image installs
    Stockfish from the base distribution's package repository. The
    `stockfish` npm package (a JavaScript/WebAssembly build of the same
    engine, same licence) backs the test suites and serves as a fallback
    when ENGINE_CMD is unset.

Chess board sounds
    apps/web/public/sounds/chess/ — cut from "chess pieces.wav" by
    simone_ds, Freesound #366065 (CC0 / public domain), also distributed
    on Pixabay as "chess-pieces-60890".

Chess API response shapes
    The fixtures under libs/fixtures/ follow the publicly documented
    Chess.com Published-Data API and the Lichess API. The players, ratings,
    identifiers and links in them are invented; no third party's games are
    redistributed here.

Other dependencies
    The dependency tree is declared across the workspace's package.json
    files and pinned in pnpm-lock.yaml. Notable direct dependencies:

      pg-boss             MIT
      drizzle-orm         Apache-2.0
      hono                MIT
      react, react-dom    MIT
      @tanstack/*         MIT
      react-chessboard    MIT
      @base-ui/react      MIT
      @lingui/*           MIT
      better-auth         MIT
      @badrap/result      MIT
      lightningcss        MPL-2.0

    Permissive licences (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0) are one-way compatible with
    the GPL: their code may be combined into a GPL program, and the result
    is GPL. `pnpm licenses list` prints the current, authoritative set.

